Bad Image Alt Text - Accessibility Test

        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            max-width: 1000px;
            margin: 0 auto;
            padding: 20px;
            line-height: 1.6;
        }
        .violation-section {
            border: 2px solid #d32f2f;
            margin: 20px 0;
            padding: 15px;
            background-color: #ffebee;
        }
        .violation-title {
            color: #d32f2f;
            font-weight: bold;
            margin-bottom: 10px;
        }
        .product-grid {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr));
            gap: 20px;
            margin: 20px 0;
        }
        .product-card {
            border: 1px solid #ddd;
            padding: 15px;
            text-align: center;
        }
        .article-list {
            border: 1px solid #ddd;
            margin: 10px 0;
            padding: 15px;
        }
        .chart-container {
            text-align: center;
            margin: 20px 0;
        }



    Bad Image Alt Text - Multiple WCAG 1.1.1 Violations
    This page demonstrates common image accessibility failures that prevent screen reader users from understanding image content.



        VIOLATION 1: Missing alt attribute
        These images have no alt attribute at all:

        Important safety warning icon above has no alt text!


        Financial performance chart above is invisible to screen readers!




        VIOLATION 2: Empty alt="" on informative images
        These informative images incorrectly use alt="":




        Shopping cart link above has no accessible name!



            Premium Laptop
            $1,299.99
            Add to Cart

        Product image above is essential but marked as decorative!




        VIOLATION 3: Useless/generic alt text
        These images have unhelpful alt text:


        Sales performance graph with useless alt="graph"


        Team photo with useless alt="photo"


        Company logo with filename as alt text




        VIOLATION 4: Keyword-stuffed alt text
        Images with SEO-spammed alt text:




                Blue Widget
                $29.99






        VIOLATION 5: Redundant alt text
        Images with redundant alt text that duplicates visible content:



            Photo of Dr. Eva Rostova

        Caption and alt text are identical - redundant for screen readers!



            Breaking News: Market Update
            Latest financial developments...

        Image alt duplicates the heading text!




        VIOLATION 6: Complex images needing detailed descriptions
        Charts and diagrams with insufficient alt text:



            Critical quarterly sales data chart with only alt="chart"!



        Organization chart showing company hierarchy with only alt="diagram"!




        Expected Scanner Results
        WCAG 1.1.1 Violations Found:

            6 images with missing alt attributes
            3 informative images with empty alt=""
            4 images with useless/generic alt text
            2 images with keyword-stuffed alt text
            3 images with redundant alt text
            2 complex images needing detailed descriptions

        Total Expected Violations: 20+ image alt text failures
        Confidence Level: High (these are clearly detectable patterns)
